{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":23.290000915527344,"text":"A figure walking, wearing a crown of lilies and peacock feathers. It is one of the best-known images from Crete, and also one of the most disputed. The genuine fragments are few, and the rest was filled in during the early 20th century. Some researchers think the pieces may belong to more than one figure, in which case the prince may never have existed in this form at all.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.6399999856948853},{"word":"figure","start":0.6399999856948853,"end":0.800000011920929},{"word":"walking","start":0.800000011920929,"end":1.340000033378601},{"word":"wearing","start":1.840000033378601,"end":1.840000033378601},{"word":"a","start":1.840000033378601,"end":2.359999895095825},{"word":"crown","start":2.359999895095825,"end":2.359999895095825},{"word":"of","start":2.359999895095825,"end":3.0399999618530273},{"word":"lilies","start":3.0399999618530273,"end":3.0399999618530273},{"word":"and","start":3.0399999618530273,"end":3.359999895095825},{"word":"peacock","start":3.359999895095825,"end":3.740000009536743},{"word":"feathers","start":3.740000009536743,"end":4.079999923706055},{"word":"It","start":4.5,"end":4.900000095367432},{"word":"is","start":4.900000095367432,"end":5.059999942779541},{"word":"one","start":5.059999942779541,"end":5.199999809265137},{"word":"of","start":5.199999809265137,"end":5.340000152587891},{"word":"the","start":5.340000152587891,"end":5.519999980926514},{"word":"best","start":5.519999980926514,"end":5.860000133514404},{"word":"known","start":5.860000133514404,"end":6.079999923706055},{"word":"images","start":6.079999923706055,"end":6.440000057220459},{"word":"from","start":6.440000057220459,"end":7.059999942779541},{"word":"Crete","start":7.059999942779541,"end":7.059999942779541},{"word":"and","start":7.300000190734863,"end":7.619999885559082},{"word":"also","start":7.619999885559082,"end":8.0600004196167},{"word":"one","start":8.0600004196167,